{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>What does YHWH your Elohim ask of you</b> — it continues: \"for your good.\" He says: He does not ask of you anything that is for His need, but rather for your need, in the sense of \"If you are righteous, what do you give Him?\" (Job 35:7) — rather, everything is for your good. And he said the reason: \"for to YHWH your Elohim belong the heavens and the heaven of heavens, the earth and all that is in it,\" and all of them give glory to His name. He has no need of you — only \"in your fathers He delighted, and He chose their seed after them, out of all the peoples, in you,\" for you are the choicest of their seed, and not in Ishmael and not in Esau."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:32.284274733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}